---
import StudyLayout from "../../../layouts/StudyLayout.astro";

const review = {
	slug: "gravity-coil-form-2026-11-03",
	title: "Gravity coil static form — study-quality review",
	status: "accepted" as const,
	phase: "scope" as const,
	question: "Evidence and limits of the static-form inquiry, 3 November 2026.",
};
const rows = [
	[
		"Purpose",
		"Supported",
		"The opening fixes the question of completeness alone and belonging on a ship, while preserving the chosen shape and excluding effects and mechanics.",
		"problem",
	],
	[
		"Investigation",
		"Supported",
		"02.2 established E as promising. 02.3–02.4 tested face proportions and dark material; owner feedback redirected the work to an under-ring. 02.5 compared three exposed widths and an inset ring against unchanged E.",
		"under-ring",
	],
	[
		"Alternatives and reasoning",
		"Supported",
		"M was selected from the direct ring comparison. It preserves E and adds continuity beneath the gaps without an exposed outer rim. A causal explanation for the earlier icon reading is not established.",
		"decision",
	],
	[
		"Evidence fit",
		"Supported",
		"Static vector comparisons address static construction. 02.6 extends the context to all four real hulls, with Light ions in every engine-compatible slot and M in every remaining equipment slot. Scale checks establish rendering dimensions, not aesthetic quality.",
		"sizing",
	],
	[
		"Cumulative agreement",
		"Supported",
		"1A, C, D and E remain available. E was not reshaped for the ring comparison. The earlier preference for shallow crowns was superseded by the owner’s decision to retain E, then select M.",
		"decision",
	],
	[
		"Design coherence",
		"Supported",
		"M was selected after being shown alone, above Fighter, above Wasp and under Wasp’s wing. The owner then selected 100% after the four-hull sizing comparison. This settles the static form and size, without claiming future collection or animation fidelity.",
		"sizing",
	],
	[
		"Remaining uncertainty",
		"Supported",
		"The 100% size is settled. The separate selectable fitting is explicitly static: no collection, capacity or energy draw; mass 10 is provisional. Collection behavior and effects remain outside this conclusion.",
		"readiness",
	],
	[
		"Integration implications",
		"Supported",
		"03 identifies the shared face schema, orientation conversion, 0.5 scale and existing renderer. 04 specifies shared artwork, the separately requested catalog fitting, and fleet/persistence/flight checks. The existing solar Loading coil remains separate.",
		"scope",
	],
];
---

<StudyLayout study={review}>
	<p>
		<a href="/lab/studies/gravity-coil-form-2026-11-03#decision"
			>Return to the selected design</a
		>
	</p>
	<section>
		<h2>Human judgment</h2>
		<p>
			E was described as the first version that belonged to the game, with
			on-chassis attachment still unresolved. The later reshaping experiments
			were considered useful evidence against continuing that direction. The
			owner then selected <strong>M / Inset ring</strong> and instructed the
			study to move to 03 and 04. The subsequent direction reopened exploration
			for a fleet sizing tool, retaining those sections as initial assessments.
			The owner then selected <strong>100%</strong>, finalized the study and
			authorized implementation. They explicitly chose a separate selectable
			Gravity coil with no collection behavior yet.
		</p>
	</section>
	<section>
		<h2>Agent assessment</h2>
		<p>
			Ratings assess the reasoning and evidence for this bounded static-form
			study. They do not average into a score or certify future implementation.
		</p>
		{rows.map(([criterion, rating, evidence, anchor]) => (
			<article>
				<h3>
					{criterion} · {rating}
				</h3>
				<p>
					{evidence}{" "}
					<a href={`/lab/studies/gravity-coil-form-2026-11-03#${anchor}`}>
						Study evidence ↗
					</a>
				</p>
			</article>
		))}
	</section>
	<section>
		<h2>Rendering checks and limits</h2>
		<p>
			The 02.5 working-tree check passed the production build, type checks and
			targeted formatting/lint. Browser inspection confirmed that all 20 new 1×
			views have matching CSS and drawing dimensions, every proposal reuses E
			unchanged, and Wasp’s one and Fighter’s four engine slots are fitted.
			Narrow-screen geometry retains its native dimensions and scrollable
			comparison.
		</p>
		<p>
			The 02.6 browser inspection covered the shared slider, keyboard steps,
			maximum-size overlaps, above-hull comparison and reset. All twelve views
			updated together. The four native canvases remained 120 × 140 CSS pixels
			on desktop and at a 390-pixel viewport, with one drawing unit per pixel.
			The fleet contains 1/3/4/5 Light ions and 2/1/2/3 coils on
			Wasp/Scout/Fighter/Corvette respectively. These are rendering and control
			checks; the subsequent human decision selected 100%.
		</p>
		<p>
			Those earlier checks concern the study page, not promoted artwork. Full
			regression and backend checks were not rerun for the ring-comparison
			round. The new 02.6 fixture draws M on Canvas with production hulls,
			engine artwork and mount transforms, including Scout, Corvette and 0.65
			flight views. It does not promote M into the shared utility artwork.
			Earlier steps 02.1–02.4 are collapsed; 02.5 and 02.6 remain visible.
			Run-local logs and screenshots are under
			<code>artifacts/gravity-coil-form/</code>; these ignored files are local
			evidence, not a durable backup.
		</p>
		<p>
			The implementation keeps all 86 M faces, their colours and paint order,
			with a 0.5 default scale. The preserved study retains the Fighter mount
			positions used for review; the production fleet follows the separate
			subsequent mount handoff. The fitting is available locally in the builder
			and flight, with no collection behavior. Run-specific implementation
			checks are recorded alongside the earlier evidence; passing them does not
			constitute publication or acceptance of future mechanics.
		</p>
		<p>
			Implementation checks passed: 132 unit tests, 33 browser tests, type
			checks, contracts, production build and targeted lint. Browser inspection
			also covered the actual catalog and test flight, and confirmed true 1×
			fleet views on desktop and at a 390-pixel viewport. Full-repository lint
			still reports formatting in the two pre-existing Wasp/1A reference SVGs.
			Backend and competition checks were not rerun for this local artwork and
			catalog change. The study is accepted; the implementation is local and has
			not been published.
		</p>
	</section>
</StudyLayout>
